dim]   Bead: [#87AFFF][/dim]sase-ps[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Page: [#87AFFF][/dim]https://github.com/sase-org/sase--beads/blob/main/pages/sase-ps/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]README.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim]  1 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Occupancy rule and live admission gate[/bold #D7AFFF]                        [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]count[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]count: separate slot occupancy from slot admission in the pure [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]runner-slot core, make a serial agent family hold one slot while any of [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]its shells (agent or monitor) is live, and wire the live admission gate [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]to the new count.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  2 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Occupancy parity across ACE and agent listings[/bold #D7AFFF]                [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]display[dim] · [dim][/dim]after count[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]display: make the ACE capacity chip, statistics methodology text, wait [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]modal, and agent listings report the same occupancy the admission gate [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]enforces, including rows for post-handoff family shells that are [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]invisible today.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  3 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Rust core parity for historical runner occupancy[/bold #D7AFFF]              [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]stats[dim] · [dim][/dim]after count[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]stats: update the duplicated runner-eligibility predicate in the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]sase-core Rust crate so the Statistics runner-occupancy analysis uses [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]the same rule as live admission, then release the binding and repin it [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]here.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  4 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Documentation sweep and cross-surface consistency check[/bold #D7AFFF]       [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]docs[dim] · [dim][/dim]after count, display, stats[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]docs: retire the \"serial family follow-ups do not consume slots\" claim [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]everywhere it appears, document the sase-agent occupancy rule and the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]monitor handoff, and verify every surface agrees end to end.[/#D7D7AF]","clan_tribe":"epic","epic_bead_id":"sase-ps","llm_provider":"claude","model":"sonnet","patch_name":"gh_sase-org__sase","phase_bead_id":"sase-ps.1","reasoning_effort":"xhigh","vcs_provider":"GitHub"},"source_run_id":"run-64edab0e2e6adf28522ec523387a7159","started_at":"2026-08-18T14:21:09.199569+00:00","state":"active"},{"commits":[],"dismissed_at":null,"files":{"commits":{"digest":"375c05a9f3a1b6662cb626f29ff2b035a765a5c46f74dc25039cdb2d49250734","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-ps.2/commits.json","size_bytes":89},"meta":{"digest":"c838480988ee1ae723fb02036c57a650df9a4b161a8efa34c794b4f7fe77fe30","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-ps.2/meta.json","size_bytes":633},"prompt":{"digest":"402b1a2c82d12e997f8fdde3f8334a827ada9813f5f335fe9977d3d943cb0525","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-ps.2/prompt.md","size_bytes":141},"state":{"digest":"ff7a6180677e6a16d0dd37c84a05cc474dbc24cdb04f882378fc17eb9303bc37","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-ps.2/state.json","size_bytes":163}},"finished_at":null,"global_name":"bbugyi200.athena.sase-ps.2","local_name":"sase-ps.2","metadata":{"agent_clan":"sase-ps","agent_clan_generation":"20260818102050","approve":true,"bead_id":"sase-ps.2","changespec_name":"gh_sase-org__sase","cl_name":"gh_sase-org__sase","clan_tribe":"epic","epic_bead_id":"sase-ps","llm_provider":"claude","model":"sonnet","patch_name":"gh_sase-org__sase","phase_bead_id":"sase-ps.2","reasoning_effort":"xhigh","vc